%% Factory resilience — PM sessions rotate through the PM thread; builds do not die with them.
%% The PM thread is the unit of ownership. A PM session is only its current occupant.
%% Section 6 is the same idea applied to addressing: a session *name* is a seat too.
%% Companion to flow-factory (the build→review cycle itself).

sequenceDiagram
    participant PM1 as PM · outgoing<br/>(context exhausted)
    participant PM2 as PM · successor<br/>(same thread)
    participant router as router.ts
    participant lifecycle as session-<br/>lifecycle.ts
    participant server as bridge-<br/>server.ts
    participant bus as event-bus.ts
    participant factory as factory.ts
    participant builder as Builder<br/>(own thread)
    participant dispatch as bridge-<br/>dispatch.ts
    participant sessions as sessions.ts

    Note over PM1,builder: build fb-N in flight (building or reviewing)

    rect rgb(238, 246, 238)
    Note over PM1,factory: 1. Gentle death — `kill` or crash
    PM1->>router: kill
    router->>lifecycle: killSession(outgoing PM)
    lifecycle->>lifecycle: registry.delete(session)<br/>registry.deleteThread(pmThread)
    lifecycle->>bus: emit session:death
    bus->>factory: factorySessionDeath
    factory->>factory: onBuilderDeath(sessionId)<br/>(separate concern — no-op for a PM)
    factory-->>PM1: 🏭 PM session ended · N builds in-flight<br/>formatBuildLine per build
    Note over factory,builder: builds map, reverse lookups and the PM thread's<br/>progress board all stay. No kill, no review cancel.
    end

    rect rgb(240, 243, 250)
    Note over factory,builder: 2. The gap — builders are self-sufficient
    builder->>factory: factory_done → review starts
    factory-->>PM1: 🏭 notifications keep landing in the PM thread<br/>(read by whoever occupies it next)
    end

    rect rgb(245, 240, 248)
    Note over PM2,builder: 3. Adoption — a successor takes the seat
    PM2->>lifecycle: respawn in pmThread
    PM2->>server: bridge registers (also on every reconnect)
    server->>bus: emit session:bridge-registered
    bus->>factory: factoryAdopt(sessionId, threadId)
    factory->>factory: builds where pmThreadId matches<br/>AND pmSessionId no longer in registry
    factory->>factory: state.pmSessionId = successor
    factory->>builder: [system] PM session replaced.<br/>New PM: name
    factory-->>PM2: 🤝 Adopted N builds
    Note over factory: idempotent — fires on every reconnect,<br/>finds nothing once pmSessionId is live
    end

    rect rgb(250, 244, 240)
    Note over PM2,factory: 4. Thread-scoped authorization
    PM2->>factory: factory_accept / retry / abandon
    factory->>factory: authorizePmThread —<br/>registry.get(caller).threadId === state.pmThreadId
    Note over factory: passes whether or not adoption ran:<br/>membership authorizes, adoption only routes
    Note over factory,builder: if no session ever decides, a 24h TTL on awaiting_pm<br/>closes the ticket and says so. The builder stays alive.<br/>Adoption inherits the clock — it does not restart it.
    end

    rect rgb(252, 238, 238)
    Note over PM2,builder: 5. Explicit destruction — `kill!` or `kill --cascade`
    PM2->>router: kill!
    router->>factory: factoryCascadeKill(sessionId)
    factory->>factory: transition failed · logBuild
    factory->>factory: cancelRun (if reviewing)
    factory->>lifecycle: killSession(builder) per build
    factory->>factory: cleanupState — drops builderSessionToTicket<br/>(same synchronous frame)
    router->>lifecycle: killSession(successor PM)
    lifecycle-->>bus: emit session:death — LATER: killSession<br/>awaits a gateway.send before emitting
    bus->>factory: factorySessionDeath → onBuilderDeath
    factory->>factory: exits at `if (!ticket)` — the reverse lookup<br/>is already gone, so nothing is reported as a crash
    Note over router,factory: no "is this kill intentional?" flag exists, or is needed:<br/>a retired build is unreachable to the death handler by construction
    end

    rect rgb(240, 246, 250)
    Note over PM2,sessions: 6. Addressing follows the seat — send_to_thread redirect
    builder->>dispatch: send_to_thread(target: "glyph")<br/>the name of the PM that died
    dispatch->>sessions: resolveSendTarget("glyph")
    sessions->>sessions: no live session by that name →<br/>rank threads by when "glyph" last sat there<br/>(registry deadAt, then thread sessionHistory)
    sessions-->>dispatch: { session: successor, replaced: "glyph" }
    dispatch->>PM2: delivered to the seat's current occupant<br/>(sender told it was redirected)
    Note over dispatch,sessions: undefined only when no thread "glyph" held<br/>has a live occupant — then the send fails as before
    end
